# Study 53 workload, sourced by run_load.sh (and read by lib_load.sh). Fixed in the design
# (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-18-study-53-glm53-kv-offload-idle-sessions-design.md) from the
# 2026-11-18 spike (docs/spikes/2026-11-18-glm53-offload-reload/); never changed once the study starts.
# Long, mostly idle coding sessions: SHARED_PROMPT tokens of system prompt shared by every session,
# USER_CONTEXT tokens of the session's own context (the repository it loaded), then turns of ISL
# input and OSL output tokens, history re-sent every turn, one turn per session every
# SECONDS_PER_TURN s. 40 sessions of ~125-130k tokens = ~5.2M tokens of history, 1.4x the GPU KV
# cache (3.77M tokens): between two turns a session is evicted from the GPU, so a resumed turn is
# either read back from the CPU offload or recomputed (~11-22 s at ~9.6k tokens/s of prefill).
SHARED_PROMPT=20000   # tokens, shared by every session
USER_CONTEXT=100000   # tokens, per session
TURNS=10              # turns per session: a session outlives the run (10 x 600 s), apart from
                      # AIPerf's shortened first sessions (the same in every experiment: same seed)
ISL=4000              # input tokens added per turn
OSL=400               # output tokens per answer (ignore_eos; reasoning included)
SECONDS_PER_TURN=600  # one turn per session every 600 s; creation = 40 x ~100k uncached tokens over
                      # the first 600 s = ~6.7-8k tokens/s, under the ~9.6k prefill rate
SESSIONS=40           # two clients x 20
# Conversations per client: 20 users, each <= 2 conversations in a run. AIPerf 0.11.0 writes
# --num-dataset-entries whole conversations to inputs.json (2000 x ~1M tokens = 8.6 GB evicted the
# clients in the spike): DATASET_ENTRIES = CONVERSATIONS (~200 MB).
CONVERSATIONS=40
DATASET_ENTRIES=40
# One AIPerf run per experiment: LOAD_SECONDS (+60 s grace), summarized on requests started >=
# STEADY_FROM s after the first request (creation done; the Akamas trim is [710s, 60s]).
LOAD_SECONDS=1500
STEADY_FROM=700
SLO_TTFT_MS=5000      # reported only (resumed turns): the score is server-side in Akamas
SLO_ITL_MS=50         # reported only
# Request fields added to every chat completion (AIPerf --extra-inputs, key:value pairs).
EXTRA_INPUTS="ignore_eos:true"
